                        "rating":  1,
                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "I\u0027m not sure if the owner has some misunderstanding about green curry chicken. Online searches suggest that green curry, also known as koryu (English: green curry), is called koryu kuen (Thai: แกงเขียวหวาน, kɛːŋ kʰǐaw wǎːn) in Thai, and is a type of Thai soup. The main ingredients of green curry include coconut milk, various spices, green chilies, garlic, galangal, lemongrass, coriander root, shallots, palm sugar, Thai eggplant, fish sauce, lime, kaffir lime leaves, and Thai basil.\n\nWhat I had for lunch today wasn\u0027t green at all, nor did it have a coconut milk flavor; it was cumin-flavored. The side dishes today included cabbage, glass noodles, bok choy, and dried tofu. The overall side dishes were too salty, and the chicken pieces weren\u0027t actually chicken cubes; there were chicken wings and bone-in meat mixed in. Overall, I think one star is too much.",
                                     "languageCode":  "en-US"
                                 },
                        "originalText":  {
                                             "text":  "不知道老闆對於綠咖哩雞丁是不是有什麼誤解，網路上查詢綠咖哩又稱青咖哩（英語：green curry），泰語名為甘綠羹（泰語：แกงเขียวหวาน，kɛːŋ kʰǐaw wǎːn），是一種泰國羹。 綠咖哩的主要成分包括椰奶、各種香料、綠辣椒、大蒜、高良薑、香茅、香菜根、紅蔥頭、棕櫚糖、泰國茄子、魚露、青檸、箭葉橙葉和泰國羅勒等食材。\n今天中午吃到的既不是綠色也沒有椰奶香是孜然口味，菜色今日配才高麗菜冬粉 油菜 豆干 ，整體配菜偏鹹，雞丁也不是雞丁裡面出現了雞翅膀跟帶骨的肉，整體下來給予一顆星我還覺得太多",
                                             "languageCode":  "zh-Hant"
                                         },
